    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbundu">Mbundu</a> kingdom in the highlands of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a> whose rulers’ title, ngola, gave the country of Angola its name.</li><li>From 1579 it fought Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>, winning at Lukala in 1590 but seeing its capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabasa">Kabasa</a>, sacked after 1617.</li><li>Queen Njinga resisted from 1624 to 1656, allied with Matamba, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imbangala">Imbangala</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pungo-andongo">Pungo Andongo</a> fell in 1671.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The ‘20. and odd’ Africans landed in English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> in August 1619 were probably captives from Portuguese campaigns against Ndongo, shipped from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> on a slave ship bound for Veracruz.</p></aside>
    </section>

